# Code owners for AprilNEA/OpenRoadie.
#
# This is a personal repository, so every owner must be an individual account
# with write access — `@org/team` entries do not exist here, and an owner
# without write access is silently ignored by GitHub. Grant write access
# before adding someone below.
#
# The LAST matching pattern wins. The order is deliberate: a broad default,
# then delegated paths, then the high-risk paths that always narrow back to
# the maintainer.

# ── Default ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*                               @AprilNEA

# ── Windows port ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Listed file by file rather than by a `*windows*` glob: in this repo the word
# means two different things, and `roadie-gui/src/windows.rs` is the app's
# auxiliary-window registry (Settings, Add Device), not Win32 code.
#
# Windows-only branches living in multi-platform files (roadie-agent's
# main.rs / autostart.rs / binary_watch/ / takeover.rs, hid/transport.rs,
# hook/lib.rs, …) stay with the maintainer: CODEOWNERS scopes by path, so it
# cannot hand out ownership of a single `#[cfg(windows)]` branch.
#
# The installer manifest (packaging/windows) and the signing workflow also stay
# with the maintainer — see the supply-chain block below.
/crates/roadie-agent/src/resume_windows.rs    @AprilNEA @davidbudnick
/crates/roadie-agent/src/tray_windows.rs      @AprilNEA @davidbudnick
/crates/roadie-camera/src/capture_windows.rs  @AprilNEA @davidbudnick
/crates/roadie-camera/src/com_windows.rs      @AprilNEA @davidbudnick
/crates/roadie-camera/src/uvc_windows.rs      @AprilNEA @davidbudnick
/crates/roadie-hid/src/transport/windows.rs   @AprilNEA @davidbudnick
/crates/roadie-hid/src/windows_hid.rs         @AprilNEA @davidbudnick
/crates/roadie-hook/src/windows.rs            @AprilNEA @davidbudnick
/crates/roadie-inject/src/inject/windows.rs   @AprilNEA @davidbudnick

